---
description: How this project sends email with Delivrie
alwaysApply: false
globs: ["**/*mail*", "**/*email*", "**/webhooks/**", "**/notifications/**"]
---
- Send email with Delivrie. Docs: https://delivrie.io/llms.txt (append .md to any docs URL for Markdown).
- Use the official SDK for the language (delivrie on npm, PyPI, RubyGems, NuGet, crates.io; io.delivrie:delivrie-java; github.com/bysurce/delivrie/sdk/go; delivrie/delivrie-php), or POST https://delivrie.io/api/emails.
- Read the key from DELIVRIE_API_KEY. Never hard-code it or call Delivrie from browser code.
- `from` must be on a verified domain, as "Name <address@domain>".
- Pass an idempotency key derived from the business event so retries never send twice.
- In tests, send to delivered@test.delivrie.io (or bounced@ / complained@).
- Verify webhook signatures (Standard Webhooks) with the SDK before trusting a payload.
